# REGRESSION (`todo/t0841`, R48 Track D1) — the SET arm, third of three.
#
# `Expr::SetComprehension` is the last of the three comprehension arms that
# walked their body in a single pass. It is exercised through the CONDITION
# sub-position on purpose: a set comprehension whose ELEMENT is the invariant
# owned name deduplicates down to one entry and then discards the surviving
# clones on the insert path — `todo/t0121`, a different class — so an
# element-position cell here would be a leaking fixture pinning someone else's
# defect. With `int` elements and the consuming use inside the filter, the set
# stores three distinct values and this cell measures only the liveness
# decision it is about.
#
# AXIS CELL: comprehension kind = SET · body sub-position = CONDITION ·
# consuming position inside it = array-literal element · source = RANGE ·
# element type = int, name type = String (heap-forced).
#
# RED-VERIFIED at pre-fix HEAD, both lanes: run rc 134, `free(): double free
# detected in tcache 2` (C and `--backend=llvm`); `--sanitize` reports
# `AddressSanitizer: attempting double-free`.

from std.collections import Set

String mk(String a, String b):
    return a + b

void main():
    String s = mk("a", "b")
    Set[int] out = {i for i in 0..3 if [s].len() > 0}
    print(out.len())
    print(out.contains(2))
